      "sequence_position": 14,
      "problem": "$$\n\nCalculate $\\int ({e}^{x}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(1-{x}^{2})})\\text{d}x$  for $|x|<1.$",
      "worked_solution": "The derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ({e}^{x}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5(1-{x}^{2})})\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\int \\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={e}^{x}-\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
